    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d757">

                <pb facs="1035" n="1025" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/8–2445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-24T21:00:00+03:00">August 24, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 24—8:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3045. <hi rendition="#italic">Red Fleet</hi> August 23 contains first mention
                    Soviet press since Soviet occupation Manchuria of “Chinese National Flag”,
                    reporting it raised over Fuyuan, near Khabarovsk first time many years. Harbin
                    crowds shouted “Hurrah” for Soviet and “Chinese peoples”.</p>
                <p>These brief references were overshadowed by descriptions of gratitude to Russians
                    and Stalin<anchor n="63" xml:id="d757-f1"/> whose portrait displayed most
                    prominently. (Sent Department, repeated Chungking 109). No mention Chiang
                        Kai-shek.<anchor n="64" xml:id="d757-f2"/> Conclusion one story reported
                    people shout “Thank you, Stalin”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d757-f1" n="63" xml:id="d757-f1-content">
                <p>Marshal Iosif Vissarionovich Stalin, Chairman of the Council of Commissars
                    (Premier) of the Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d757-f2" n="64" xml:id="d757-f2-content">
                <p>Generalissimo and President of the National Government of the Republic of
                    China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
